WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:03.940
You walked the girls home for me.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.890
Want to come in for a bit?

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.160
There's something I want 
to talk to you about.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.460
How's it going, delivering the flyers?

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.340
It's a bit rough.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.390
I thought it would be.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.720
You think it's a bit weird, don't you?

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:44.700
If they want an audience, why don't 
they ask their friends first, right?

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.230
Yeah.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.080
It might be my fault.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:56.360
I like my life right now, so I really 
don't want anyone to make fun of me.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:04.210
Because of that, I've always avoided 
making friends with people at school.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:09.100
I think I might have given them the 
idea that they shouldn't do anything

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.830
to risk letting their 
special place be desecrated—

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:14.110
that they don't need other friends—

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:19.290
that the three of them only need each other.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:24.140
I figure this is good enough for me.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:25.770
But...

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:30.440
There's no reason that those 
girls need to live the same way.

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:34.940
It might turn out that 
no one makes fun of them.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.590
Maybe they'll hold a concert 
at the church and have a blast

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.440
with their friends from school.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.440
Maybe there's a chance they'll have a future

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.700
where they'll have made some happy memories.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:48.330
If there is, I want them to choose that path.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.460
Why don't you...

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.630
No way.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.900
It's something that I'm not allowed to say.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:03.220
I'm the very person who's 
meandered my way through life.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.600
If <i>I</i> told them,

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.980
I'd win an award for hypocrisy of the week.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:25.830
<i>That church—Little Wing—
is filled with kind people.</i>

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.370
<i>They know what happiness looks like to them,</i>

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.840
<i>but they care so much about each 
other that they can't step in.</i>

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:42.340
<i>But there might be things that 
I can tell them as an outsider.</i>

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:52.680
Recorder

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:52.680
Player

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.680
I just came up with a song.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.690
It just kind of came to me, 
despite the situation.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.690
Or maybe it's <i>because of</i> the situation.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.450
Now I just need lyrics.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.950
<b>Concert</b>

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.330
We still have a lot left.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.820
What can you expect?

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:15.210
We had practice, and we had 
to do band practice first.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.460
We can try harder tomorrow.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.710
Hey, girls,

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.090
don't you think school...

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.920
I'd win an award for hypocrisy of the week.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.350
Hypocrisy, huh?

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:49.320
You met with the girls again today, huh?

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.670
Yeah.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:51.580
I guess.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.580
You don't spend time with me, 
but you do with them, huh?

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.590
That's why I'm serving you right now.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.090
I-I'm not letting you 
pretend that's good enough.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.340
Kurumi,

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.730
I'll start going to school tomorrow.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:16.730
I see.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.120
That's not anything special.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.670
It's what you're supposed to do.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:41.880
Let's see...

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.510
Is this right?

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.750
Good luck.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.750
Thanks, Kurumi.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:39.960
<i>If I don't take a step forward, 
I can never connect.</i>

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:47.730
<i>If I have a goal to reach, nothing will 
happen until I move towards it myself.</i>

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:52.990
<i>That's what I want to teach 
Jun, Nozomi, and Sora.</i>

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:59.190
<i>But I don't have the right 
to say such a thing.</i>

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:05.580
<i>So I'm going to go earn that right myself.</i>

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:26.860
<i>Hang in there.</i>

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:32.870
Also, if you haven't handed in your 
assignment yet, please do so by tomorrow.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:39.870
About the schedule for the midterm exams...

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:36.110
Three, two, one...

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.240
Rock n' roll!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:40.870
Who's that?

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:43.170
Who's that?

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:44.390
P-Pardon me.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.020
U-Um...

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.380
You're... Uh...

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.700
N-Nukui Kyo.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:53.380
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.240
Nukui-kun?

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.140
Student number 17?

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:58.440
Yes.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.140
Probably.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.870
I-I see.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.520
Please be careful from now on.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.890
I understand.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.020
Sorry.

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:08.530
Hey, Sensei...

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:10.020
Y-Yes?

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.070
May I sing a song?

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.400
What? Why?

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.690
As a self-introduction and a notice.

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:21.850
I won't ever do such a thing again.

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:23.660
May I, please?

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:28.790
I don't know, now's not the time.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.290
Why not?

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:33.860
Toriumi-san?

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:36.910
Why not? It's only once.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.390
He comes to school for the first time,

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.630
a month late, with a guitar, 
asking to be allowed to sing.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:43.300
How weird can you get?

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.870
He's so weird that I'm 
actually curious to hear.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:47.890
She has a point.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.880
Sensei, I want to hear him, too.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:51.690
Same here.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.870
P-Please quiet down, everyone.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:03.170
Also, Sensei, he might get 
violent if you turn him down.

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:07.080
Please show us your performance, Nukui-kun.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.360
N-Nice to meet you.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:15.880
Belatedly, I'm Nukui Kyo, 
a fellow student in your class.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.770
I've decided to come to 
school as of today.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:20.220
Thanks for having me.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.610
Why do you have a guitar with you?

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.880
I-It's my hobby.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.110
I like making music.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:36.670
The people I'm indebted to are going 
to be performing my music live.

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:41.010
So if you hear my music, and you like it,

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:44.490
I'd be grateful if you'd 
come see them perform.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:48.250
So please, allow me play just one song.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:03.540
<i>I finally found</i>

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:06.770
<i>All these things</i>

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:13.650
<i>Let's just walk as far as we can</i>

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:20.530
<i>Even if you have a feeling 
you'll lose even more</i>

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:27.160
<i>Just live the best you can 
and color your emotions</i>

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:35.460
<i>I want to roar how beautiful the world is</i>

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.820
Th-Thank you very much.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:46.750
The actual concert is 
going to be much better.

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:48.430
I hope you come to watch.

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.470
<i>I can't be running away.</i>

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.990
<i>Worse, I ended up so hurt 
that I ended up sleeping in.</i>

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:11.460
I-It's evening already?

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:18.340
Yo.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.510
It's me, Kyo.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.070
Hey, you're finally here.

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:23.590
<i>I've been waiting for you.</i>

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.360
Thank you for having me.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.890
<i>Isn't this...</i>

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:33.990
Yeah, I brought it here.

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:35.400
Along with this.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:46.760
S-Sorry, but, why?

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:51.220
I thought on my feet, 
and I recorded it for you.

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:52.120
You need it, don't you?

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.690
Of course not, how could I need it?

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:56.460
You do need it.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:01.090
How are you going to express how committed 
you are if you don't show this to them?

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:06.420
Sakura told me, more or less, what's going on.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.220
Sorry for everything.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.830
I'm sorry, too.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:14.600
You told me to help them give up, and yet...

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.850
The kids are practicing downstairs.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:21.620
Do for us what we can't do.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:29.740
Master's music is easy to play, 
but it's kind of boring.

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:34.500
It's surprisingly hard 
to play slowly, though.

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:38.840
Kyo-san.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:42.210
Girls, there's something 
we need to talk about.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:53.470
Didn't you say you were quitting when 
you started your orphanage work?

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:57.480
Yeah, but he's taking care of it now.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:00.690
So I'm taking a little breather.

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:05.190
Jun. Nozomi. Sora.

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:07.700
I have a proposal.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:13.580
Why don't we try asking your classmates 
if they can come to the concert?

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.980
You can just talk to them casually.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.050
If we want the concert to work,

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:23.090
I think we should talk to 
the people around us first.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:25.840
But...

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:33.100
Hey, do you love this place, Little Wing?

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.860
O-Of course I do.

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:36.030
I love it.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:38.690
But... That's why...

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.060
What about you, Jun and Sora?

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:43.450
I love it.

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:45.310
I do, too.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:49.790
That's why I want to do something 
memorable, one last time.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.320
But...

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:55.330
In that case, why don't 
you think of it like this:

00:14:56.120 --> 00:15:01.640
there might be other people who 
will come to love this place.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:04.340
Other people, besides us?

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:10.720
I was really happy when you told me when 
you told me that you like my music.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:18.110
So doesn't it excite you to 
think about the possibility

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:24.270
of your friends coming to 
love your performance here?

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:26.810
I think they'll like it.

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:33.860
I already love this church, 
and I love Little Wing.

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:38.620
I can't help but want 
to see you perform here.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.120
Kyo-san...

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:43.530
You don't have to decide right away.

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:49.170
You can have plenty of 
time to think about it.

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:54.550
I'll keep helping you with 
practice until the concert.

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:59.090
I'm going to do what I can, until it's done.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.230
G-Good morning.

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:13.240
I thought you might stop coming again, 
after what happened yesterday.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:19.550
After what I told the girls, 
I decided I have to do what I can.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:21.090
Well done.

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:24.620
A sticker?

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:41.060
It's starting to sound pretty good.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:45.060
Okay, want to go hand out the flyers?

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:54.070
We aren't handing out the 
flyers at the station anymore.

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:01.400
I got a flyer at school today.

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:04.220
Stop looking at me, pervert!

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:05.540
S-Sorry.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:12.300
I finally know what you were 
up to with those girls.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:16.430
You could have said something.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:17.680
Then...

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:21.140
I told you to stop looking at me!

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.650
Set List

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:27.650
Let's see...

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:31.000
Assuming we're doing roughly 
ten songs at the concert...

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:34.040
We've got at least five 
of today's songs ready.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.150
That many?

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:40.540
We can do Judy and Mary's 
"Blue Tears" and "Rubber Soul,"

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:42.490
since we practiced them 
when we started the band.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:46.160
We can also do about three of 
the songs that Master wrote.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:47.540
Oh, yeah?

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:51.390
We have enough songs then, 
so we just need to decide on the order.

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:53.210
U-Um...

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:57.510
Th-There's another song that I 
want to do at the concert.

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:01.570
The one you sang at school.

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:04.690
Y-You saw that video?

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:05.530
Yes.

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:09.520
Master showed it to us, 
saying, "This is true rock."

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:14.280
I-I thought that song was really good.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:19.910
So I want to sing it, too.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.280
<b>Strawberry
Au Lait</b>

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:25.740
Looks like those girls are 
practicing really hard.

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:26.460
Yeah.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.790
They're starting to sound really good.

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:34.170
It was Jun who said she wanted to do the 
song that you sang at school, right?

00:18:34.740 --> 00:18:36.450
She seemed to really like it.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:38.460
She insisted on singing it.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.430
I liked that song, too.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:44.990
I always have.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:49.020
You always have?

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.910
<b>Little Wing
Concert today
Guitar & Vocals: Goto Jun
Bass: Momijidani Nozomi
Drums: Kaneshiro Sora</b>

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:38.070
So this is where those girls live.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.320
Wow.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.450
It's so nice inside.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.890
Let's go, Kurumi.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:43.610
Yeah.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:53.880
I know. No kidding.

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:03.630
So many people.

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.300
H-Here we go, Jun.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:06.430
Y-Yeah...

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:08.910
What's wrong?

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:10.770
Go, already.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:12.880
Y-You go, Zomi.

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:15.270
I'll go when you go.

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:28.390
Jun, Sora, here we go.

00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:09.490
That was awesome!

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:11.970
That was great!

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:19.980
<i>I don't want this moment to end.</i>

00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:24.030
<i>There's no way I can let this end, 
after just this time.</i>

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:24.960
<b>The World Is but Rock n' Roll</b>

00:23:25.690 --> 00:23:29.320
Dear Lord, we come today to thank you.

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:41.000
<b>#05: It's so fun taking pictures of you, 
because you don't realize how cute you are.</b>

00:23:29.320 --> 00:23:31.160
For allowing us to hold 
such a beautiful concert.

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:33.450
For allowing us to meet Kyo-san.

00:23:33.450 --> 00:23:36.870
Thank you very, very, much.

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:39.010
Thank you.
